  "prompt": "Image 1 is the exact character identity and art reference: Noct four-star form \"Da Anh Kiem Si\", a chibi hooded shadow swordsman in clean HD smooth painted game art (NOT pixel art). Keep him exactly: soft pointed black hood, completely black hidden face with ONLY two small luminous pale lavender-violet eyes, dark scarf, dark gunmetal forearm and shin guards half swallowed by a long layered black half-robe and torn cloak whose ragged edges are lined with deep violet, small dark boots; ONE long single-edged BLACK CRESCENT MOON-BLADE (strongly curved like a crescent moon, blackened steel, thin pale silver-violet edge, dark wrapped grip, small round guard). NO scythe, NO dagger, NO second weapon, NO silver chest plate, NO visible face or skin.\nImage 2 is a scale-and-root template made from the same accepted character. Preserve Image 2 exact cell locations, fixed camera distance, standing-equivalent anatomical scale, body-root position at the horizontal center of each cell, grounded foot-contact line at about 94% of cell height, and padding. Change only the action pose in each slot. Never zoom or resize a pose to fill its cell. Hood, torso, robe, boots and blade size must stay identical to Image 2 in every frame. Do not reproduce Image 2 as-is and do not draw any guide, border or separator.\n\nCreate a 6-frame ATTACK animation sheet: a fast two-cut crescent-blade combo, body only. Frame 1: ready guard, blade held diagonally in front of the body with the tip pointing down near his front boot. Frame 2: wind-up, blade drawn back up over his left shoulder, body coiled, cloak tatters swinging back. Frame 3: rising diagonal slash, blade swung up in front of the body to the upper right, arm extended forward, lean forward. Frame 4: reverse downward slash, blade cutting down across the front toward the lower right, body twisting. Frame 5: low follow-through crouch, blade ending low in FRONT of him near his right boot, tip pointing down, cloak snapping forward. Frame 6: recover to the ready guard of frame 1 (blade tip down near the front boot).\n\nBLADE CONTAINMENT (most important): the curved blade is the only long object. Imagine an invisible safe box covering the central 84% of every cell (8% margin on each side). The ENTIRE blade, from pommel to tip, plus the whole body and cloak, must stay inside that safe box in EVERY frame. During swings bend the elbow and keep the blade close to the body or angled up/down instead of reaching sideways; never let the tip point horizontally toward a neighbouring cell. Nothing from one frame may appear in another cell.\n\nFacing RIGHT in 3/4 view in every frame. Body plus blade only: NO slash arc, NO weapon trail, NO motion lines, NO particles, NO sparks, NO smoke, NO aura, NO afterimages, NO magic circle (effects are separate runtime layers). Keep the blade compact and close to the body so it stays fully inside its own cell; leave a clear magenta margin of at least 5% on all four sides of every cell. Same camera distance and same body scale in all 6 frames; body center stays near the cell center; feet stay on the same ground line except where noted.\nExactly 6 frames in a 3 columns x 2 rows grid of equal square 512x512 cells, total image 1536x1024, read left-to-right then next row. Background 100% solid flat #FF00FF magenta in every cell, no gradient, no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no numbers, no gridlines, no borders, no frames between cells. Clean HD smooth painted, NOT pixel art.\n",
